8. Embodied Action IR

A candidate intermediate representation should avoid encoding morphology unless morphology is causally relevant.

An action object might contain:

ActionIR {
    agent_goal
    initial_world_state
    desired_world_state
    target_objects[]
    object_relations[]
    affordances[]
    contact_requirements[]
    force_constraints[]
    motion_constraints[]
    spatial_constraints[]
    causal_operator
    trajectory_class
    temporal_dependencies[]
    prerequisite_skills[]
    termination_condition
    failure_conditions[]
    confidence
    provenance
}

Example:

ActionIR {
    agent_goal: OPEN(drawer_1)
    target_objects:
        drawer_1
        handle_1
    affordance:
        handle_1 -> grasp_or_hook
    contact_requirement:
        controllable_contact(handle_1)
    motion_constraint:
        drawer_1 translates along axis X
    causal_operator:
        apply_force(handle_1, +X)
    termination_condition:
        drawer_1.displacement >= desired_distance
}

Nothing here requires fingers.

That omission is intentional.

