12. Provenance and Epistemic Weighting

Each learned experience should retain information about its source.

A minimal structure:

Experience {
    source_type
    source_identity
    extraction_method
    inferred_or_observed
    physical_reliability
    social_reliability
    temporal_reliability
    embodiment_gap
    confidence
}

Possible source classes:

REAL_ROBOT
HUMAN_REAL_WORLD
ANIMAL_REAL_WORLD
SIMULATION
VIDEO_GAME
INSTRUCTIONAL_MEDIA
FICTION
SYNTHETIC_VIDEO

Knowledge is therefore not simply accumulated.

It is weighted.

A fictional sequence may contribute a useful hypothesis without becoming a trusted physical law.

